expression: help
---
Run multiple prompts in one resident Apple M4 CPU/NEON SLM session

Usage: bitnet mac chat [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Configuration file path

      --model-family <MODEL_FAMILY>
          Model family for the resident chat route. BitNet requires --bitnet-chat-gate-receipt

          Possible values:
          - dense-slm: Run the supported dense Qwen SLM resident chat path
          - bitnet:    Run the gate-required accepted BitNet M4 CPU/NEON chat route

          [default: dense-slm]

  -d, --device <DEVICE>
          Device/backend label (cpu, cuda/gpu, hip/rocm, oneapi, npu/openvino-npu, nvidia-rtx-5070-ti-cuda/wgpu, intel-a770-opencl, metal/mpsgraph, apple-m4-metal, apple-m4-mpsgraph, apple-m4-cpu-neon, apple-m3-air-metal, apple-m3-air-mpsgraph, apple-m3-air-cpu-neon, auto). Apple M4 and M3 Air labels are distinct proof lanes

      --prompt <TEXT>
          Prompt to answer. Repeat for each turn in the resident Mac session

      --log-level <LEVEL>
          Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)

      --stdin
          Read additional prompts from stdin, one non-empty line per turn

      --interactive
          Collect prompts from an interactive line loop until /exit, /quit, or EOF

      --batch-size <SIZE>
          Batch size for processing

      --model-id <MODEL_ID>
          Supported model id. Defaults to the validated Apple M4 SLM runtime artifact

          [default: qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q8_0]

      --model-path <PATH>
          Explicit accepted BitNet GGUF path. Only used with --model-family bitnet

      --tokenizer <PATH>
          Explicit accepted external BitNet tokenizer path. Only used with --model-family bitnet

      --bitnet-chat-gate-receipt <PATH>
          Ready BitNet chat gate receipt required before --model-family bitnet can run

      --cache-dir <PATH>
          Override model cache root. Defaults to ~/.cache/bitnet-rs/models

      --system <TEXT>
          Optional system prompt

      --max-new-tokens <MAX_NEW_TOKENS>
          Maximum new tokens to generate per prompt

          [default: 64]
          [aliases: --max-tokens, --n-predict]

      --temperature <TEMPERATURE>
          Temperature for sampling. The Mac wrapper defaults to deterministic greedy

          [default: 0]

      --top-k <TOP_K>
          Top-k sampling. The Mac wrapper defaults to greedy top-1 behavior

          [default: 1]

      --top-p <TOP_P>
          Top-p sampling

          [default: 1]

      --repetition-penalty <REPETITION_PENALTY>
          Repetition penalty

          [default: 1.1]

      --seed <SEED>
          Random seed for reproducibility

      --threads <THREADS>
          Number of CPU threads to use (0 = all cores; deterministic mode may override)

          [default: 0]

      --no-stream
          Do not stream generated token text to stdout

      --progress
          Emit operator progress lines to stderr while keeping token text on stdout

      --quiet
          Suppress warm-session status/progress lines; token streaming still uses stdout

      --no-turn-receipts
          Disable per-turn receipt files; the aggregate session receipt still records each turn

      --allocation-audit
          Include scoped hot-loop allocation counter deltas in session receipts

      --metal-prefill-qkv-phase
          Route the validated Q/K/V prefill Metal phase as an opt-in contribution; answers remain CPU/NEON

      --json-out <PATH>
          Output aggregate Mac chat session receipt

          [default: target/apple-m4-continuity/mac-chat.json]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
